    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0586" n="458" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">572.F1/264: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Delegation to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1928-09-24T10:00:00-04:00"
                            notBefore="1928-09-22T00:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>].<lb/>[Received September 24, 1928—10
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>7. Eighth and last plenary session Telegraph Conference Saturday ended with
                    signing of protocol containing amendments to Paris regillations <pb facs="0587"
                        n="459" xml:id="pg459"/> effective October 1929. New regulations maintain
                    ten-letter code word at present rate and definitely state conditions to which
                    they must conform. New conditions will not cause scrapping present codes.
                    Amended regulations also provide for new category of five-letter code words with
                    no restrictions as to formation at two-thirds present charge in extra European
                    regime and three-fourth present charge in European regime. Under latter category
                    unions of plain-language words in five-letter groups also admitted. Amended
                    regulations will therefore not increase cost telegraphic communication to
                    anybody, if anything slight decrease may result from new class five-letter
                    words. Full report being prepared and work of delegation will be completed by
                    September 27. Report will be forwarded by next Embassy pouch.<anchor n="94"
                        xml:id="d323-f1"/> Account crowded conditions Embassy unable to arrange
                    return passage earlier than October 5th and has approved allowance subsistence
                    to that date.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>]
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Del</hi>[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >egation</hi>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
